\description{
Builds a multimodal transport network from a directory with one
'OpenStreetMap' extract (\code{.pbf}), zero or more 'GTFS' feeds (\code{.zip})
and, optionally, an elevation raster (\code{.tif}). The network lives in
memory and is reused by every routing function; nothing is written to
\code{data_path}. The files are recognised by their extension in lower case
only: a \code{map.PBF} or a \code{feed.ZIP} is ignored.
